E
"fur"
"This pile of animal furs stands about three feet high.  Certainly yeti and

fade furs are in the pile, as well as some tanned hides.

"
E
"bone"
"Hundreds of bones, large and small, lie in a stack about two feet in height. 

Some are large enough to have come from the stone giants themselves; others

are small enough to be from a jay or other local bird.

"
E
"north heap rock"
"A jumbled heap of rocks lies stacked against the northern wall of this

chamber.  Most are closer in size to a boulder than a pebble.

"
E
"south bow"
"A single bow similar to those used by the elven hunters in the Vaasa lies broken by the southern wall.

"
